{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2117","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Lost Soul"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two integer arrays $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$, each of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may perform the following operation any number of times: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose an index $$$i$$$ $$$(1 \\le i \\le n - 1)$$$, and set $$$a_i := b_{i + 1}$$$, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"or"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" set $$$b_i := a_{i + 1}$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Before"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" performing any operations, you are allowed to choose an index $$$i$$$ $$$(1 \\le i \\le n)$$$ and remove both $$$a_i$$$ and $$$b_i$$$ from the arrays. This removal can be done "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at most once"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let the number of matches between two arrays $$$c$$$ and $$$d$$$ of length $$$m$$$ be the number of positions $$$j$$$ $$$(1 \\le j \\le m)$$$ such that $$$c_j = d_j$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to compute the maximum number of matches you can achieve."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains an integer $$$t$$$ $$$(1 \\le t \\le 10^4)$$$ — the number of test cases. The description of each test case follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$n$$$ $$$(2 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5)$$$ — the length of $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ $$$(1 \\le a_i \\le n)$$$ — the elements of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\dots, b_n$$$ $$$(1 \\le b_i \\le n)$$$ — the elements of $$$b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single integer — the answer for the test case."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n4\n1 3 1 4\n4 3 2 2\n6\n2 1 5 3 6 4\n3 2 4 5 1 6\n2\n1 2\n2 1\n6\n2 5 1 3 6 4\n3 5 2 3 4 6\n4\n1 3 2 2\n2 1 3 4\n8\n3 1 4 6 2 2 5 7\n4 2 3 7 1 1 6 5\n10\n5 1 2 7 3 9 4 10 6 8\n6 2 3 6 4 10 5 1 7 9\n5\n3 2 4 1 5\n2 4 5 1 3\n7\n2 2 6 4 1 3 5\n3 1 6 5 1 4 2\n5\n4 1 3 2 5\n3 2 1 5 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3\n0\n4\n3\n5\n6\n4\n5\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, we can do the following: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" We will choose not to remove any index. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$3$$$, and set $$$a_3 := b_4$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [1, 3, 2, 4]$$$, $$$b = [4, 3, 2, 2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$1$$$, and set $$$a_1 := b_2$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [3, 3, 2, 4]$$$, $$$b = [4, 3, 2, 2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$1$$$, and set $$$b_1 := a_2$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [3, 3, 2, 4]$$$, $$$b = [3, 3, 2, 2]$$$. Notice that you can perform $$$a_i := b_{i + 1}$$$ and $$$b_i := a_{i + 1}$$$ on the same index $$$i$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The number of matches is $$$3$$$. It can be shown that this is the maximum answer we can achieve."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, we can do the following to achieve a maximum of $$$3$$$: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Let's choose to remove index $$$5$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [2, 1, 5, 3, 4]$$$, $$$b = [3, 2, 4, 5, 6]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$4$$$, and set $$$b_4 := a_5$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [2, 1, 5, 3, 4]$$$, $$$b = [3, 2, 4, 4, 6]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$3$$$, and set $$$a_3 := b_4$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [2, 1, 4, 3, 4]$$$, $$$b = [3, 2, 4, 4, 6]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$2$$$, and set $$$a_2 := b_3$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [2, 4, 4, 3, 4]$$$, $$$b = [3, 2, 4, 4, 6]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$1$$$, and set $$$b_1 := a_2$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [2, 4, 4, 3, 4]$$$, $$$b = [4, 2, 4, 4, 6]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$2$$$, and set $$$b_2 := a_3$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [2, 4, 4, 3, 4]$$$, $$$b = [4, 4, 4, 4, 6]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose index $$$1$$$, and set $$$a_1 := b_2$$$. The arrays become: $$$a = [4, 4, 4, 3, 4]$$$, $$$b = [4, 4, 4, 4, 6]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, it can be shown that we can not get any matches. Therefore, the answer is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"2117E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2117/problem/E"}